This product includes software developed by other projects.

1. JSqlParser 5.3

   Used by the rendering engine jar (`engine/`, built from the IntelliJ
   repository) to parse SQL when checking dialect and performance rules.

   JSqlParser is dual-licensed under LGPL-2.1 and Apache-2.0. This project uses
   it under the Apache-2.0 branch only; the LGPL branch is not used, and no
   LGPL obligation attaches to the distributed package. A copy of the
   Apache-2.0 text is in LICENSE.

   Project: https://github.com/JSQLParser/JSqlParser

2. openidea-plugin SDK 0.1.51 (project API 1.15)

   Linked at build time from https://github.com/l0ng-ai/openidea at tag
   v0.1.51. Its licence and notices are those of the OpenIDEA repository.

3. mps-sql-agent.jar

   Built from the IntelliJ repository's `sub-projects/sql-visualizer-agent` and
   bundled at `agent/mps-sql-agent.jar`, because `[[contributes.javaAgents]]`
   only accepts a jar inside the package. It relocates ASM (BSD-3-Clause)
   under the agent's own namespace.

4. PostgreSQL JDBC Driver 42.7.1 (BSD-2-Clause) and Microsoft JDBC Driver for
   SQL Server 12.4.2.jre11 (MIT)

   Shipped inside the engine jar (`mpsv-engine-<version>.jar`, downloaded at
   first use and verified against `engine/ENGINE_VERSION.sha256`) so the
   sidecar can run a read-only EXPLAIN against PostgreSQL or SQL Server.

   Projects: https://jdbc.postgresql.org/ and
   https://github.com/microsoft/mssql-jdbc

   Project: https://github.com/OW2/asm

5. IntelliJ expui icon set (Apache-2.0)

   The SVGs under `icons/` (the plugin logo, the two tool-window icons and the
   toolbar set in `icons/toolbar/`) are taken from the IntelliJ plugin's own
   resources, which use JetBrains' IntelliJ Platform UI icon set (expui). They
   are distributed under Apache-2.0; a copy of that text is in LICENSE.

   Project: https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community